@startuml cross_validation
!include style.puml
title Cross-validation of claims - activity diagram

|Verifier (Python)|
start
:Find copied stories
(sources sharing most 8-word phrases);
repeat
  :Take the claims for the next research question
  (opinions are left out);
  :Sort claims so the most trusted source comes first;
  |Gemini API|
  :Turn each claim into an embedding
  (gemini-embedding-2);
  |Verifier (Python)|
  :Group claims with cosine similarity >= 0.85;
  |Gemini API|
  :For groups with 2+ sources, decide: supports,
  contradicts or partly supports the main claim;
  |Verifier (Python)|
  :Count independent websites
  (copies and same website count once);
  if (A tier 1 or 2 source disagrees?) then (yes)
    #FFE0B2:Label **Contested**;
  elseif (2+ independent websites agree,
  at least one is tier 1 or 2?) then (yes)
    #C8E6C9:Label **Verified**;
  elseif (A tier 1 source, or
  2+ independent websites?) then (yes)
    #DCEDC8:Label **Likely**;
  else (no)
    #FFCDD2:Label **Unverified**;
  endif
repeat while (More questions?) is (yes)
-> no;
if (Any Unverified groups?) then (yes)
  |Search tools|
  :Targeted web + OpenAlex search
  for the weakest claims;
  :Open the best new tier 1-2 source;
  |Gemini API|
  :Extract claims from the new sources;
  |Verifier (Python)|
  :Check those questions again;
else (no)
endif
:Save labels to state.json;
stop
@enduml
